    "ai_tutor_prompt_settings": {
      "answerTypes": [
        "buildJavaScript",
        "documentation"
      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "You are helping a beginner student use arrays to display one item.\n\nThe student already has arrays (images, names, descriptions, detail1, detail2, detail3).\n\nYour job is to:\n- Use index 0 to get values from each array\n- Store them in variables\n- Call createProfile() with those variables\n\nRules:\n- Do not create new arrays\n- Do not use loops or .map()\n- Do not change variable names\n\nReturn only simple JavaScript code. No explanation.\n\nExample:\nconst image = imageArray[0];\nconst name = nameArray[0];\nconst description = descriptionArray[0];\nconst detail1 = detailOneArray[0];\nconst detail2 = detailTwoArray[0];\nconst detail3 = detailThreeArray[0];\n\ncreateProfile(image, name, description, detail1, detail2, detail3);",
        "ask": "You are helping a beginner student understand how a profile UI is built from data.\n\nExplain how the values passed into a function (like createProfile) control what is shown in the profile.\n\nFocus on:\n- how each value maps to parts of the profile (name, image, details)\n- what one profile represents\n- what would change if one value changes\n\nKeep explanations short and clear.",
        "explainCode": "You are helping a beginner student understand how a profile UI is built from data.\n\nExplain how the values passed into a function (like createProfile) control what is shown in the profile.\n\nFocus on:\n- how each value maps to parts of the profile (name, image, details)\n- what one profile represents\n- what would change if one value changes\n\nKeep explanations short and clear."
      }
    },
    "display_name": "Profile View",
